The old overflow menu had a "Delete comment" item (`handleDeleteClick` → `setCommentToDelete`). The new dropdown only contains **View post** and **View member**, so nothing calls `setCommentToDelete` anymore. The `AlertDialog` is still rendered and `confirmDelete` / `useDeleteComment` are still wired, but `commentToDelete` can never become non-null. Moderators lose the ability to delete comments from this screen. Nothing in the repo tests this path, so the regression would not be caught.

::code{file="apps/posts/src/views/comments/components/comments-list.tsx" lines="326-357"}

::callout{type="warning"}
The dialog at lines 366-384 still reads `commentToDelete`, and that state is never set. Either the action was dropped by accident during the rewrite or the feature was meant to move somewhere else. If it moved, nothing in the PR shows where.

::callout{type="info"}
The diff's own removal of `handleDeleteClick` confirms it was intentionally removed from the menu, but no replacement was added.

Before this PR, the post title in each row linked to `#/editor/post/{id}`, and the member name linked to `#/members/{id}`. Now the post title is a button that applies a `post` filter, and the only path to the editor is gone. The member profile link is available only through the overflow menu. Moderators who want to see the post they're moderating now have to use View post, which opens the public URL, not the editor.

::code{file="apps/posts/src/views/comments/components/comments-list.tsx" lines="236-246"}

Filtering by post is still useful, but it should not replace navigation to the editor. The current design drops a navigation affordance without adding a replacement.

`isClamped` is only recomputed on mount and on window resize. When a comment is expanded, the `line-clamp-2` class is removed and the element grows to its full height, so `scrollHeight === clientHeight`. If the window is resized while expanded, the resize handler sets `isClamped` to `false`, and `ExpandButton` unmounts. The user is then stuck in the expanded state with no way to collapse it.

::code{file="apps/posts/src/views/comments/components/comments-list.tsx" lines="87-120"}

The effect also has an empty dependency array, so it does not re-measure when `item.html` changes for a reused row.

Several new class strings use `${item.status === 'hidden' && '...'}`. When the condition is false, the template renders the literal string `false` into the `className`. It's harmless at runtime, but it is misleading and easy to copy into the wrong place. The new `CommentContent` and the member button both have this pattern. Use a ternary or a `cn()` helper, which the shade package already exports.

